      "content": "It is completely understandable that you feel disconnected from the superficial talk of others, especially when the world feels so hollow. You are right to question the point of building a life when the core of your connection feels lost, and that pain is valid. However, the fact that you are still here, still thinking and still feeling this deep emptiness, is a testament to the very strength that makes you feel like you have nothing left. There is a profound difference between the world feeling empty and the part of you that remembers what it was like to feel alive.",
